@startuml e2e_result_evaluation
title E2E result evaluation and consumer views

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 12

start

:Sender: encode E2E header
(Counter + CRC + Data ID);
:Transport / binding;
:Receiver: decode & verify E2E header;

if (DataIntegrityCheckEnabled?) then (yes)
    :data_integrity:
    kOk / kError;
else (no)
    :data_integrity:
    kDisabled;
endif

if (DataIntegrityCheckEnabled\nAND data_integrity == kError?) then (yes)
    :sequence:
    kDisabled
    (check skipped, no new enum value);
    note right #Yellow
        Bypass: the counter of a corrupted
        sample is not trustworthy, so the
        sequence check is skipped. The
        data-integrity error is fed directly
        into historical health.
    end note
else (no: kOk or check disabled)
    if (SequenceCheckEnabled?) then (yes)
        :sequence:
        kOk / kOkGapWithinThreshold
        / kErrorRepeated / kErrorGapExceedsThreshold;
    else (no)
        :sequence:
        kDisabled;
    endif
endif

if (HistoricalHealthTrackingEnabled\nAND at least one check enabled?) then (yes)
    :Hysteresis check
    (pass/fail of enabled checks only,
    data-integrity error only on bypass);
    :historical_health:
    kOk / kError;
else (no)
    :historical_health:
    kDisabled;
endif

-> inputs: data_integrity,\nsequence, historical_health;
:summary:
kDisabled / kOk / kOkWithDisabledChecks / kError
(aggregated from data_integrity,
sequence and historical_health);
note right #Yellow
    kError: at least one enabled check failed
    (data_integrity, sequence or historical_health)
    kOk: all checks enabled and passed
    kOkWithDisabledChecks: enabled checks passed,
    some checks disabled
    kDisabled: nothing was checked
end note

:SamplePtr::GetE2EResult()
returns E2EResult{data_integrity, sequence,
historical_health, summary};
note left #Yellow
    Reduced view:
    the consumer checks only the
    summary field.
end note
note right #Yellow
    Detailed view:
    the consumer inspects data_integrity,
    sequence and historical_health
    individually for full diagnostics.
    These fields are always returned,
    independent of historical health.
end note

stop
@enduml
